      },
      "worked": "For $g$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=6-x\\\\x&=6-y\\\\y&=6-x\\\\g^{-1}(x)&=6-x\\end{align*}$$\nFor $h$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{3}{x}\\\\x&=\\frac{3}{y}\\\\xy&=3\\\\y&=\\frac{3}{x}\\\\h^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{3}{x},\\quad x\\ne0\\end{align*}$$\nEach function is its own inverse, so each is an involution. Both $h$ and $h^{-1}$ have domain $\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
